# Fictional EP Tracklist

## Track 1: Canister 8 Changes on the Inhale

**Story & Context:** At 134 BPM, Rina holds a compact five-note shō cluster through alternating exhale and inhale states. Darius assigns kick plus mono bass to EXHALE and snare plus short vocal cuts to INHALE. The first Breath Flip lands late in beat two, so Reverse Accent forces the next kick response away from the downbeat. Emi adds one prepared-Rhodes suspended-second dyad after every second full breath cycle. Junpei marks only the longest reversals with a dry woodblock. In the middle section, Reed Continuity Test removes drums and bass while Rina crosses from inhale back to exhale without breaking the chord.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Brass pneumatic canister stamped 8 beside a pressure chart with arrows marked IN and OUT, one continuous pale waveform crossed by a red vertical switch line, fluorescent reflection on cream tile. Sparse lyric fragments: “canister eight,” “change on inhale,” “same chord,” “floor moves.”

## Track 2: The Chute Holds One Breath Too Long

**Story & Context:** At 138 BPM, the track centers on Airline Hold. Rina extends an EXHALE state beyond the expected four-bar cycle, forcing Darius to keep the kick-and-bass arrangement active while the snare family remains withheld. The delay creates tension because the audience expects the next rhythmic state but cannot receive it until Rina reverses naturally. When the Breath Flip finally arrives, Junpei lands one shime-daiko rim stroke and Malik enters with a low contrabass-clarinet fall. A later Continuous Chord / Broken Floor section leaves the shō unchanged while the drums fracture into half-bar kick bursts and empty beats.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Steel document chute with a paper canister stopped midway, pressure gauge needle held above a red mark, a long horizontal breath arrow extending past four numbered boxes. Sparse lyric fragments: “hold the chute,” “one breath long,” “not yet,” “turn now.”

## Track 3: IN Lamp, OUT Lamp, No Final Kick

**Story & Context:** The closer runs at 128 BPM and begins with shō, contrabass clarinet air, and one dry snare every two bars. Darius gradually introduces the club floor, but every breath direction carries a different partial arrangement. EXHALE has kick and bass; INHALE has snare, vocal cut, and prepared-piano punctuation. As the track develops, Rina shortens the breath states so the machine arrangement flickers more rapidly. In the final minute, the opposite happens: she sustains one exceptionally long inhale while the chord remains stable. Darius progressively removes kick doubles until only one expected final kick remains. Rina reverses breath just before it. Reverse Accent cancels the cadence, and the EP ends on the continuing shō cluster, one woodblock click, and room air.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Dark sorting room after shutdown, two red panel lamps labeled IN and OUT, one still glowing beside a silent drum machine, shō resting near a brass tube manifold, blank final square on a rhythm card. Sparse lyric fragments: “in lamp,” “out lamp,” “no final kick,” “keep the air.”

